---
import { PLATFORMS_DATA } from '../data/platform-metadata';

const platforms = Object.values(PLATFORMS_DATA);
---

<section class="py-20 bg-[#0e0e0c] border-t border-white/5">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
    <div class="text-center max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-12">
      <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-amber-500 mb-2">
        Social Media & Messenger
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">
        Schriftarten für deine Lieblings-Plattformen
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-stone-400">
        100% kompatible Unicode-Textstile für Instagram Bio, TikTok, WhatsApp Status, Discord Server und mehr.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Platform Cards Grid -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
      {platforms.map((p) => (
        <a
          href={p.slug}
          class="bg-[#141412] border border-white/10 hover:border-amber-500/40 rounded-2xl p-5 transition-all hover:-translate-y-1 group flex flex-col justify-between"
        >
          <div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-3">
              <span class="text-2xl">{p.icon}</span>
              <div>
                <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white group-hover:text-amber-400 transition-colors">
                  {p.name}
                </h3>
                <span class="text-[11px] text-stone-400">Limit: {p.bioLimit} Zeichen</span>
              </div>
            </div>

            <p class="text-xs text-stone-400 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              {p.tagline}
            </p>

            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1 mt-2">
              {p.compatibleStyles.slice(0, 3).map((st) => (
                <span class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded bg-white/5 text-[10px] text-stone-300">
                  {st}
                </span>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-4 pt-3 flex items-center justify-between text-xs text-stone-400 group-hover:text-amber-400 font-semibold border-t border-white/5">
            <span>Zur {p.name}-Anleitung</span>
            <span class="group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform">→</span>
          </div>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>

    <!-- Inline Explainer: Native App Formatting vs. Unicode Generator (Gap 5 Differentiator) -->
    <div class="mt-10 bg-amber-500/5 border border-amber-500/20 rounded-2xl p-6 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start gap-4">
      <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-amber-500/20 text-amber-400 flex items-center justify-center text-xl shrink-0">
        💡
      </div>
      <div class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-stone-300 leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-white font-semibold block mb-1">
          Wichtig: Native App-Formatierung vs. Unicode Schriftarten
        </strong>
        Viele Apps wie WhatsApp bieten eigene Formatierungen über Steuerzeichen (z. B. <code class="text-amber-400 font-mono bg-black/40 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">*fett*</code> oder <code class="text-amber-400 font-mono bg-black/40 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">_kursiv_</code>). Diese Formatierung funktioniert jedoch nur lokal in der jeweiligen App. Unser Unicode-Generator erzeugt echte universelle Schriftzeichen, die auch beim Kopieren in Instagram, Discord, E-Mails oder Gaming-Profile exakt im gewünschten Look erhalten bleiben.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
